<http://data.silknow.org/object/5582d0c7-59d6-3db8-91c3-8cbdfb289645>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Brocaded in silver wire wound on a silk core, silver frisé yarn and polychrome silks on a cream-colored satin ground. Large sprays of fruits and flowers, and rococo panels with landscapes, brocaded in polychrome silks. Remainder of surface entirely covered with brocading in silver in a pattern of vines of oak leaves and acorns. Selvedge on part of one side of six cords and one stripe. Worn."@en ;
